---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — CosmoCrew"
  description="How the CosmoCrew website handles your data — the short version: no cookies of our own, no analytics scripts, no trackers. We only see aggregate visit counts."
  path="privacy"
>
  <section class="container narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        How this website handles your data — the short version: no cookies of
        our own, no trackers, only aggregate visit counts.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Prose>
      <p><em>Last updated: 26 October 2026</em></p>

      <p>
        This policy covers the CosmoCrew website (<strong>cosmocrew.dev</strong> and
        its GitHub Pages address). For the apps themselves, see <em>Our apps</em> below.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        No personal information of our own. This is a static website. Our pages
        set no cookies, run no analytics scripts in your browser, and contain no
        advertising or third-party trackers. We don&rsquo;t ask for or store any
        personal information ourselves. Our hosting providers process standard
        request data to serve the site, and Cloudflare may set a strictly
        necessary security cookie when it has to check that a visitor is not a
        bot; both are described under <em>Hosting</em> below. The only thing we
        look at is aggregate visit counts.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>. Like any web host,
        GitHub may process standard technical information (such as your IP address
        and browser request data) in order to deliver the site and protect its
        service. That processing is governed by <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub&rsquo;s Privacy Statement</a>.
        At cosmocrew.dev the site is also served through <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which,
        like any web host, handles standard request data such as your IP address,
        the page you requested and the site that referred you. That processing is
        governed by <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Cloudflare&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.
        From Cloudflare we look only at aggregate visit counts (which pages were
        visited, which sites referred visitors, and from which countries), never
        at individual visitors or IP addresses.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us at <a href="mailto:contact@cosmocrew.dev">contact@cosmocrew.dev</a>,
        we receive your message and email address (routed to our inbox via
        Cloudflare Email Routing) and use them only to reply. We don&rsquo;t add
        you to any mailing list.
      </p>

      <h2>Our apps</h2>
      <p>
        The CosmoCrew apps are separate from this website. Each app&rsquo;s data
        practices are described in its App Store privacy details, on its
        support page or, for the web app, on its website:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>SliceFocus</strong> — <a href="https://slicefocus.app" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">slicefocus.app</a></li>
        <li><strong>LexiPower</strong> — <a href="https://cosmocrew.dev/lexipower-support/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">support page</a></li>
        <li><strong>With Handlebars</strong> — <a href="https://withhandlebars.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">withhandlebars.com</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, we&rsquo;ll update the date at the top of this page.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: var(--maxw-prose);
  }
</style>
